  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN. You can perform the following operation on it any number of times (possibly, zero):\n\n\nChoose any index iii (1≤i≤N1\\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N) and change AiA_iAi​ to 000.\nYour goal is to maximize the value of the maximum subarray sum of AAA.\n\nFind the **minimum number of operations** needed to achieve this.\n\nNote that an **empty subarray** has a sum of 000.\n\nFormally,\n\n\nFor any pair of integers (L,R)(L, R)(L,R), let s(L,R)s(L, R)s(L,R) denote the subarray sum function, where:\n\nIf 1≤L≤R≤N1 \\leq L \\leq R \\leq N1≤L≤R≤N, then s(L,R)=AL+AL+1+…+ARs(L, R) = A_L + A_{L+1} + \\ldots + A_Rs(L,R)=AL​+AL+1​+…+AR​\nOtherwise, s(L,R)=0s(L, R) = 0s(L,R)=0.\n\n\nFor the array AAA, define f(A):=max⁡(s(L,R))f(A) := \\max (s(L, R))f(A):=max(s(L,R)) across all pairs (L,R)(L, R)(L,R) of integers.\n\nThis is the maximum subarray sum of array AAA.\nYour goal is to make f(A)f(A)f(A) as large as possible by performing the given operations on the array AAA.\n\nFind the minimum number of operations needed to achieve this goal.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN — the number of elements in AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum number of operations required to achieve the maximum possible subarray sum.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100",
      "−100≤Ai≤100-100 \\leq A_i \\leq 100−100≤Ai​≤100",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 4⋅1054 \\cdot 10^54⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n-1 -3 -4\n3\n1 -1 1\n5\n1 2 -1 -2 4",
        "output": "0\n1\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The current maximum subarray sum is 000, obtained by taking the empty subarray.\nIt can be shown that no matter how we perform operations, this will not change.\nSo, no operations need to be done, and the minimum number of operations required is 000.\nTest case 222: Change A2A_2A2​ to 000 using the operation, making the array [1,0,1][1, 0, 1][1,0,1].\nThis will make the maximum subarray sum 222, which is the maximum possible.\nUsing 111 operation this way is optimal.\nTest case 333: Change A3A_3A3​ and A4A_4A4​ to 000 using the operation, turning the array into [1,2,0,0,4][1, 2, 0, 0, 4][1,2,0,0,4].\nThis will make the maximum subarray sum 777, which is the maximum possible.\nWe needed 222 operations to do this."
      }
    ]
